# TypeScript conventions

- `strict` is on; no `any` (use `unknown` + a type guard instead). No `!` non-null assertion
  when the case can be checked properly.
- ES modules, named exports, **no** default exports. One class per file,
  file name = class name (`Mat4.ts`). Every folder has an `index.ts`.
- Code, identifiers, comments and JSDoc in **English**. JSDoc on every public class/method,
  incl. the unit (radians, pixels) and whether the object is mutated.
- Options objects instead of long parameter lists; options have sensible defaults
  (`interface FooOptions` + `Partial`/defaults in the constructor).
- No side effects on import (the package is `sideEffects: false`).
- No `console.log` in library code.
- Formatting: 4 spaces, single quotes, semicolons.
